  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "WestPlaza Holdings sold one of its shopping centres for $\\$20\\,000\\,000$ and invested the money at a daily compound interest rate of $0.016\\%$. How much interest did the company earn in the first year? Use 365 days in a year and give your answer to the nearest cent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$1\\,202\\,680.28$\n\nCompound daily for 365 days, then subtract the original investment.",
      "worked": "The daily rate is $R=0.016\\div100=0.00016$, and $n=365$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{365}&=P(1+R)^{365}\\\\A_{365}&=20\\,000\\,000(1.00016)^{365}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}I&=A_{365}-P\\\\I&=20\\,000\\,000(1.00016)^{365}-20\\,000\\,000\\\\I&\\approx\\$1\\,202\\,680.28\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe company earned $\\$1\\,202\\,680.28$ in interest, to the nearest cent.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
